  "$schema-note": "enabledSource: \"docblock\" = the date the flag itself records; \"floor\" = the earliest date this repository can prove, used for the fourteen flags whose real flip is recorded NOWHERE (ADR-0084). A floor can only make a flag look YOUNGER than it is, so retiring on one is conservative \u2014 never premature. It is not corrected by guessing.",
  "sizing": "A batch is sized by BLAST RADIUS. The enablement cohort only sets the EARLIEST date a flag may fall on (enabled + horizonDays); it does not set the batch. Re-spaced 2026-08-09 after the original cohort-only split put 17 flags and ~75 production files into a batch due in nine days \u2014 the largest batch on the second-earliest date.\nMEASURED per flag: production files referencing the constant, and the number of playwright*.config.ts files that PIN it. The pin count is the one nobody had: VITE_CANVAS_AUTHORING is pinned in 14 configs and VITE_SCHEDULING_MODES in 13, and CI proved a single pinned config costs six specs to convert, not a line.\nESTIMATED, and labelled as such: weight = files + 3x pins, a cap of 45 per batch, and a fortnightly cadence. Those three numbers come from ONE completed retirement, so they are a hypothesis rather than a plan. `check:flags` tests it for us \u2014 if batch 2 takes longer than a fortnight, the next batch date fails and forces a re-fit against a second data point. Re-fit it then; do not defend it."
